  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 927 AM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nBeautiful weather remains on tap Thursday & Friday as well with\nthe warming trend continuing as highs get into the upper-60s to\nlow-70s. Some moisture starts to work itself back into the area,\ncausing some clouds to reappear. As far as rain goes, we'll have\nto wait until the weekend...maybe. Moisture advection and a weak\nshortwave on Saturday gives us low rain chances (10-15%) with \nanother shortwave and cold front Sunday resulting in slightly \nbetter rain chances (15-20%). Definitely still some model \ndisagreements, but moisture advection ahead of the front doesn't \nlook that impressive. Forecast rain totals right now over the \nweekend are less than 0.20\" with a low probability of exceeding \nthat. Dry conditions return early next week behind the front with \ncooler temperatures as well with highs in the 50s and lows in the \n30s.",
